export default {"T000614":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Krull dimension at most zero ∧ Quasi-separated ⇔ Hausdorff underlying space</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000048\"><span>Krull dimension at most zero</span><code>P000048</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000035\"><span>Quasi-separated</span><code>P000035</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000614\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000614</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000049\"><span>Hausdorff underlying space</span><code>P000049</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> In dimension zero, quasi-separatedness makes the intersection of two affine charts a quasi-compact open in a profinite space, hence clopen there. The Stacks criterion gives Hausdorffness. Conversely Hausdorffness gives dimension at most zero and makes every affine chart closed, so affine intersections are quasi-compact.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CKV\">Stacks 0CKV · zero-dimensional schemes</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/properties/#tag-0CKV\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000614\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000614\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000615":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Krull dimension at most zero ∧ Qcqs scheme ⇒ Affine</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000048\"><span>Krull dimension at most zero</span><code>P000048</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000046\"><span>Qcqs scheme</span><code>P000046</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000615\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000615</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000031\"><span>Affine</span><code>P000031</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> A quasi-separated scheme of dimension zero has affine quasi-compact opens by the cited lemma. Apply this to the whole scheme. The empty scheme is the spectrum of the zero ring.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CKV\">Stacks 0CKV · zero-dimensional schemes</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/properties/#tag-0CKV\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000615\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000615\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000669":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Finite ⇔ Affine ∧ Proper</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000019\"><span>Finite</span><code>P000019</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000669\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000669</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000017\"><span>Affine</span><code>P000017</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000023\"><span>Proper</span><code>P000023</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> A finite morphism is affine, of finite type, separated and universally closed. An affine universally closed morphism is integral, and integral morphisms of finite type are finite.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WN\">Stacks 01WN · finite if and only if affine and proper</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01WN\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000669\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000669\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000670":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>H-projective ⇒ Projective ∧ H-quasi-projective</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000471\"><span>H-projective</span><code>P000471</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000670\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000670</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000020\"><span>Projective</span><code>P000020</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000473\"><span>H-quasi-projective</span><code>P000473</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> A closed immersion is quasi-compact, and projective space is the projective bundle of a finite free module.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01W9\">Stacks 01W9 · H-projective implies both properties</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01W9\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000670\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000670\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000671":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Projective ⇒ Locally projective</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000020\"><span>Projective</span><code>P000020</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000671\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000671</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000472\"><span>Locally projective</span><code>P000472</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Take the singleton open cover of the target.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01W8\">Stacks 01W8 · projective variants</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01W8\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000671\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000671\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000672":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Locally projective ⇒ Proper</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000472\"><span>Locally projective</span><code>P000472</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000672\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000672</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000023\"><span>Proper</span><code>P000023</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Properness is local on the target. On a sufficiently fine affine cover, the restricted morphism is a closed subscheme of projective space.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WC\">Stacks 01WC · locally projective morphisms are proper</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01WC\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000672\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000672\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000673":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>H-quasi-projective ⇒ Quasi-projective</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000473\"><span>H-quasi-projective</span><code>P000473</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000673\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000673</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000021\"><span>Quasi-projective</span><code>P000021</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The quasi-compact immersion gives finite type over the base and the restriction of the twisting sheaf is relatively ample.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VY\">Stacks 01VY · H-quasi-projective morphisms are quasi-projective</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01VY\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000673\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000673\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000674":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Quasi-projective ⇒ Locally quasi-projective</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000021\"><span>Quasi-projective</span><code>P000021</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000674\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000674</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000474\"><span>Locally quasi-projective</span><code>P000474</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Take the singleton open cover of the target.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VW\">Stacks 01VW · quasi-projective variants</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01VW\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000674\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000674\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000675":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Locally projective ⇒ Locally quasi-projective</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000472\"><span>Locally projective</span><code>P000472</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000675\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000675</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000474\"><span>Locally quasi-projective</span><code>P000474</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Apply projective implies quasi-projective to the same open cover of the target.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01W8\">Stacks 01W8 · projective variants</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01W8\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VW\">Stacks 01VW · quasi-projective variants</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01VW\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07RL\">Stacks 07RL · projective implies quasi-projective</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-07RL\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000675\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000675\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000676":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Locally quasi-projective ⇒ Separated ∧ Of finite type</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000474\"><span>Locally quasi-projective</span><code>P000474</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000676\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000676</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000024\"><span>Separated</span><code>P000024</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000026\"><span>Of finite type</span><code>P000026</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Both properties are local on the target and hold for quasi-projective morphisms.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VX\">Stacks 01VX · locally quasi-projective implies separated of finite type</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01VX\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000676\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000676\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000677":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Qcqs target ∧ Quasi-projective ∧ Proper ⇒ Projective</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000470\"><span>Qcqs target</span><code>P000470</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000021\"><span>Quasi-projective</span><code>P000021</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000023\"><span>Proper</span><code>P000023</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000677\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000677</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000020\"><span>Projective</span><code>P000020</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Over the qcqs target a quasi-projective morphism factors through an open immersion into a projective scheme. Properness over the common target makes the open immersion closed.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BCL\">Stacks 0BCL · part (1), proper quasi-projective morphisms over a qcqs base</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-0BCL\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000677\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000677\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000678":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Qcqs target ∧ H-quasi-projective ∧ Proper ⇒ H-projective</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000470\"><span>Qcqs target</span><code>P000470</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000473\"><span>H-quasi-projective</span><code>P000473</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000023\"><span>Proper</span><code>P000023</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000678\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000678</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000471\"><span>H-projective</span><code>P000471</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Factor through an open immersion into an H-projective scheme. Properness over the common target makes the open immersion closed.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BCL\">Stacks 0BCL · part (2), proper H-quasi-projective morphisms over a qcqs base</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-0BCL\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000678\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000678\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>"};
